    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d64">

                <pb facs="0206" n="176" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v18/pg176"/>

                <head>64. Telegram From the Department of State to the
                        Embassy in Japan<anchor n="0" xml:id="d64-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1959-05-20T13:16:00-04:00">May 20, 1959, 1:16
                            p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>1757. For MacArthur from Robertson. Deptel 1726.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d64-f2"/> Re Article XXV 2(b). We
                    agreeable to deleting Article XXV 2(b) providing for yen contribution in new
                    administrative arrangements. (FYI. As soon as we
                    have reached agreement with GOJ on all major
                    substantive points, we intend <pb facs="0207" n="177" xml:id="pg177"/> discuss
                    entire package with appropriate Congressional committees. End FYI)</p>
                <p>In interest of answering possible Congressional objections to dropping yen
                    contribution most helpful if Fujiyama
                    would affirm that GOJ intends take every
                    practicable measure assure that funds derived from absence yen contribution will
                    be used for Japanese defense forces.</p>
                <p>Defense concurs.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Dillon</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d64-f1" n="0" type="source" xml:id="d64-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 611.94/5–2059. Confidential; Niact; Limit Distribution. Drafted by Sneider on May 18; cleared with L/FE, H in
                    substance, and with DOD; and approved by
                        Dillon. Repeated to CINCPAC exclusive for POLAD and Admiral Felt, and
                    to COMUS/Japan exclusive for General
                        Burns.</p>
            </note>
